# DEMO 2: Parallel analysis (fan-out + fan-in)
#
# coordinator splits the work -> 3 agents analyze SIMULTANEOUSLY, each on its
# own specialty -> merger combines the 3 reports into a single one.
#
# What you see in the web interface:
#   - 3 pixels leave coordinator AT ONCE (fan-out) -> parallelism
#   - the 3 agents pulse at the same time
#   - the pixels CONVERGE toward merger (fan-in) -> merger waits for all
#
# The analysis takes as long as the slowest agent, not the sum of them.
#
# Run:
#   ./pixelgo flow run demo demo/02-parallel-audit.flow "Analyze src/calc.c"

entry coordinator

node coordinator
node security
node performance
node style
node merger

# FAN-OUT: 3 edges from the same node -> the 3 run IN PARALLEL
edge coordinator -> security
edge coordinator -> performance
edge coordinator -> style

# FAN-IN: 3 edges into merger -> waits for ALL, receives all reports
edge security    -> merger
edge performance -> merger
edge style       -> merger

edge merger -> END
